  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Le Jardin is at 18 ter avenue Dréo, in Brignoles, in the Var. Chef Julien Tosello, who took over the address a few years ago, serves homemade bistronomic cuisine there, based on fresh, seasonal produce, with the Maître Restaurateur title. The restaurant's website speaks of a private, tree-lined garden; the tourist office listing counts 80 seats including 40 outdoor tables, and the Gault&Millau guide describes a large town-centre space combining a garden terrace and a dining room that is often full.</p>

      <h2>Dogs: what the sources say</h2>
      <p>The restaurant's official listing on the Provence-Alpes-Côte d'Azur Tourisme portal, updated by Provence Verte & Verdon Tourisme on 23 March 2026, ticks "Animals accepted" ("Pets welcome" in the English version). It does not say whether this applies to the dining room or the terrace only, nor whether there is a limit on numbers. The restaurant's website does not mention dogs. With 40 outdoor tables, the terrace remains the simplest way to settle in with a dog, but ask when booking.</p>

      <h2>Hours, prices, booking</h2>
      <p>According to the restaurant's website, service is on Tuesday and Wednesday from 12pm to 2pm, then Thursday to Saturday from 12pm to 2pm and from 7:30pm to 10pm. The restaurant is closed on Sunday and Monday. At lunch, Tuesday to Friday excluding public holidays, the set menu changes every week: dish of the day €18, starter-main or main-dessert €22, starter-main-dessert €25. The market menu, served at lunch and dinner, is €35 for two courses and €40 for three; a five-course "Inspiration du Chef" menu at €60 is offered at dinner only. Takeaway by phone before noon is also possible on 04 94 77 00 75.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: book on 04 94 77 00 75, say you will come with your dog and ask for a table in the garden so that it stays calm during service.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>The restaurant is on avenue Dréo, in the centre of Brignoles: the official listing specifies that it is in the town centre and close to a motorway, which makes it an easy stop if you are crossing the Provence Verte with your dog.</p>
